if you're used to roadie running and  national roles gears tactics may seem a  bit unfamiliar and really tough  fortunately we here at GameSpot have  come up with a few essential tips and  strategies to help you rip apart the  Locust Horde with ease  number one not all cover is created  equal even if this is your first  tactical turn-based game you probably  know that your units should always be in  cover as you advance and flank your  enemies ensure that your soldiers are  safely tucked behind a lower high wall  before you end your turn keep in mind  that low and high walls have different  properties you can shoot over low cover  but you aren't fully protected from a  frontal attack high cover gives you full  frontal protection but you can only  target enemies at the corner of the wall  you should also be weary of destructible  wooden cover it breaks after one shot  and will knock your unit back think  carefully before you move your units one  bad move and you could lose one of your  favorite soldiers number two executions  executions executions every unit has a  set number of action points that dictate  how many actions that unit can carry out  each turn these actions include moving  firing throwing grenades and using  abilities however in Gears tactics each  time you get an execution each of your  squad members gets an extra action point  this means that as long as you keep  scoring executions you can prolong your  turn a few well-timed executions can  change the tide of battle in order to  get an execution first you need to down  an enemy to do that shoot until it drops  to its knees keep in mind that if you do  too much damage to an enemy it will die  right away  if you're near an enemy low on health to  switch to your pistol to ensure the down  number three overwatch if you're  familiar with XCOM then the term  overwatch should sound pretty familiar  basically it allows units to hold an  angle and shred an enemy that moves  within or into that units line-of-sight  overwatch is instrumental when it comes  to defense usually setting up overwatch  is the last thing you want to do in any  given turn because it will eat up all of  your units action points keep in mind  friendly fire is very much a thing in  Gears so we don't recommend setting up  overwatch directly behind another unit  if an enemy's overwatch is giving you a  hard time you can use the disabling shot  to stun them number four classes and  skill trees each unit both friendly and  low  he has a specific class called classes  come in the form of sniper support  Vanguard Paragon and heavy each class  has different abilities standard weapons  and a customizable skill tree we  recommend digging through each classes  skill trees to see how you want to  customize and develop your soldiers if  you don't like how one of your soldiers  turned out you can use respect tokens  which can be acquired throughout the  game number 5 locust classes  surprisingly traditional locust classes  and enemy types from Gears of War  translate pretty well to Gears tactics  drones are your common locust soldiers  they are fairly weak utilized range  attacks and love setting up overwatch  wretches can't take a lot of hits but  they will rush your units and claw them  because their movement is fairly  predictable overwatch can work wonders  or if you're near a group of them a  well-placed grenade can pop them like  water balloons the Grenadier is a  shirtless locust that carries a shotgun  and takes quite a few hits like wretches  they will rush you but if they manage to  pen a unit down they are much tougher to  deal with sniper drones are drones with  a lot more range if you can we recommend  taking out the snipers first these are  only a handful of enemy types you'll go  up against so pay extra attention  whenever a new one is introduced number  six loot boxes use tactics may not have  microtransactions but it still has  supply crates that contain weapon  attachments armor and cosmetics you can  earn crates by completing secondary  challenges or finding them on the  battlefield gray boxes house common loot  blue rare and purple legendary well we  do recommend going out of your way to  collect these crates be smart about when  you choose to do so rushing for these  crates can get you killed  number 7 side missions although gears  tactics is structured like your average  Gears game with acts and chapters  occasionally you will be able to embark  on side missions many of these side  quests compared with different gameplay  modifiers so be sure to check out your  mission Intel before you choose the  squad most of these missions are fairly  straightforward and offer decent rewards  but one thing to keep in mind is that  your units can only go on one side  mission per act this means that you may  want to think twice before setting out  on a mission stacked with only heroes if  you have any tips for use tactics please  leave them in the comments below and be  sure to check  our review here on YouTube or  gamespot.com thank you so much for  watching
 

